import "core"
import "/repo/dir/test/Integration/code/artifacts/catln-test/Welcome.md"
import "/repo/dir/test/Integration/code/artifacts/catln-test/Notes/Nested.md"


/Data/Note/Page(/title= "Queries")
  # Which blocks of a note are queries over its vault's tasks, and which are code.
    
    Before, [Welcome](Welcome.md).
  /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "not done")
  # After, [Nested](Notes/Nested.md). A fence written in tildes, in capitals, or with a space after the word is a query
    too.
  /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "not done")
  /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "not done")
  /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "not done")
  # A fence saying it is something else, or saying the word as part of a longer one, or saying nothing,
    is code.
    
    ```dataview
    not done
    ```
    
    ```tasksmore
    not done
    ```
    
    ```
    not done
    ```
    
    A query holding a fence is written between a longer one.
  /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "not done\n```\nsort by due")
  # An indented tasks fence is code, not a query.
    
      ```tasks
      not done
      ```
    
    A tasks fence inside a longer block is a line of that block.
    
    ````
    ```tasks
    not done
    ```
    ````
    
    A query written under a checkbox is a query of it.
  /Data/Note/Task/Simple(/contents= "Plan it", /state= /Data/Primitive/False)
    /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "not done")

  # A query saying nothing is a query.
  /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "")
  # A link written inside a query is writing about a link, and travels in the query as it was typed.
  /Data/Note/#tasks(/query= "path includes [[Welcome]]")
